name: Noto Sans Hebrew 3.000, Noto Sans Arabic 2.005, Noto Sans Devanagari 2.001, Noto Sans Symbols 2 2.003, Noto Sans Thai 2.002, Noto Sans CJK SC 2.004 (subset)
upstream: https://github.com/notofonts (hebrew, arabic, devanagari, symbols, thai), https://github.com/notofonts/noto-cjk (Sans/OTF/SimplifiedChinese)
retrieved: Hebrew / Arabic / Devanagari / Symbols 2 copied unchanged from the Ubuntu/Noto stock font set on the build box; Thai from notofonts.github.io fonts/NotoSansThai/hinted/ttf (2026-11-04, unchanged)
subset: NotoSansCJKsc-Subset.otf = NotoSansCJKsc-Regular.otf 2.004 (sha256 2c76254f6fc379fddfce0a7e84fb5385bb135d3e399294f6eeb6680d0365b74b,
        https://github.com/notofonts/noto-cjk/raw/main/Sans/OTF/SimplifiedChinese/NotoSansCJKsc-Regular.otf; the pan-CJK
        font with SC default forms) through `python make_cjk_subset.py NotoSansCJKsc-Regular.otf NotoSansCJKsc-Subset.otf`
        = pyftsubset (fontTools 4.63) --unicodes=U+1100-11FF,U+3000-303F,U+3040-309F,U+30A0-30FF,U+3131-318E,U+31F0-31FF,
        U+FF00-FFEF plus the Han characters with Unihan 15.1 kTGH index <= 1000 or kFrequency <= 2 (1382 ideographs) plus
        the 2350 KS X 1001 Hangul syllables (EUC-KR 0xB0A1-0xC8FE), --layout-features=kern,palt,halt,ljmo,vjmo,tjmo
        --no-hinting --drop-tables+=VORG,vhea,vmtx,BASE. 4576 code points, 5493 glyphs, CFF (CID). Deterministic (head
        dates come from the source). The Han / kana / punctuation glyphs, advances and vertical metrics are identical to the
        previous subset of the region font NotoSansSC-Regular.otf 2.004 (sha256 faa6c9df...5ea9), which has no Hangul
        syllables; only the name table now reads "Noto Sans CJK SC".
